      "text": [
        " سَأَلْتُ أَبَا عَبْدِ اللَّهِ ( عليه السلام ) عَنِ اسْتِلَامِ الرُّكْنِ قَالَ اسْتِلَامُهُ أَنْ تُلْصِقَ بَطْنَكَ بِهِ وَ الْمَسْحُ أَنْ تَمْسَحَهُ بِيَدِكَ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Muhammad Bin Yahya, from Muhammad Bin Al Husayn, from Safwan Bin Yahya, from Yaqoub Bin Shuayb who said, ",
          "‘I asked Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> about touching the corner (of the Kaaba). He<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘Touch it and attach your belly with it, and the wiping it that you wipe with your hand’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "1. Muhammad ibn Yahya has narrated from Muhammad ibn al-Husayn from Safwan ibn Yahya from Ya’qub ibn Shu’ayb who has said the following: “I once asked abu ‘ Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, about feeling the corner (of al-Ka‘bah). He (the Imam) replied, ‘Istilam (feeling) is touching it (the Black Stone) with your belly and al-Mash (touching) is wiping it with your hand.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
